**/database.types.ts
# Machine-generated repo inventory with a byte-for-byte CI gate (claude-config
# bin/build-directory.py --check, oss-borrow W1.4). Its own banner says
# DO-NOT-HAND-EDIT, and a formatter rewrite IS a hand edit: prettier re-aligns the
# markdown tables, after which `--check` reports the file as stale and every PR to
# that repo fails the gate. Found 2026-08-12 — the gate had ALREADY been red on
# claude-config main since the previous autofix style commit, unnoticed because the
# gate only runs on pull_request. Exact same shape as database.types.ts above: a
# generator and a formatter cannot both own one file.
DIRECTORY.md
# claude-config's claude-md/*.md are VERBATIM MIRRORS of each repo's CLAUDE.md, republished
# by its sync rail whenever a provably-current clone differs. Prettier rewriting the mirror
# GUARANTEES it differs, so autofix and sync ping-pong two commits per cycle forever —
# measured live 2026-08-13 (deep audit): iptorian.md and diplosint.md each flipped between
# the same two md5s five times in under 12 h. Fixed in claude-config (56d996e1, with a
# prettier-semantics test); mirrored here so the next autofix template sync keeps the fence.
claude-md/
# claude-config's memory/*.md are DATA, not prose: they carry Google Drive file ids, AWS secret
# names, vibration-pattern arrays and other literals whose exact bytes are the whole value.
# Prettier's emphasis normalisation cannot tell an identifier from markup, so it rewrites them
# silently — 2026-08-17 (bot 5bd9f070) turned a Drive folder id's `__` into `**` (unresolvable:
# a Drive id is [A-Za-z0-9_-] only) and `MAESTRO_QA_*` into `MAESTRO*QA*\*`, the very AWS secret
# name an operator would have provisioned from that note.
#
# THIS FENCE HAS ALREADY BEEN LOST ONCE, WHICH IS WHY IT LIVES HERE. It was added to
# claude-config's own .prettierignore on 2026-08-17 and worked — until 2026-08-20 06:38Z, when
# `chore(ci): update .prettierignore from signlo-platform-ops` (claude-config d7384d60) deployed
# THIS file over it and deleted all 17 lines. Three minutes later, at 06:41Z, `style: apply
# automated formatting fixes` (bb911d16) rewrote 12 memory files and re-escaped bold markers to
# literal \*\*. scripts/sync_autofix.py maps .github/.prettierignore -> each repo's root
# .prettierignore, so a repo-local fence on a SYNCED file is not a fence at all: it survives
# exactly until the next sync. Anything that must be ignored has to be ignored HERE.
memory/

